{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/285890-goblin-hedge-settlement-halloween-town","id":285890,"title":"Goblin Hedge Settlement: Halloween Town","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-18T07:36:48-07:00","id":285890,"title":"Goblin Hedge Settlement: Halloween Town","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_content text_table_postContainer\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postfooter text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_small text_table_postTop text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postfooter_td\" colspan=\"3\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_post text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_message text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_post_td\">This is an old project I dusted off from my &quot;toybox&quot; that I was hoping for some input on regarding improvements. Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated. &lt;3 <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Goblin Hedge Settlement: Halloween Town</span></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Found beyond the warmth of Summer, yet seen just before the tundras of Winter, there exists a settlement surrounded by gnarled black trees and graveyards. Yet despite its morose trappings, laughter and screams mingle together and echo from the place, for here there be the presence of Autumnal Nightmare and festivity. Halloween Town is a hedge settlement where by night all celebrate the traditions of Halloween, and by day prepare for the coming of the next night's jubilation. Naturally, all who use Contracts of Autumn or Spring gain a +2 to enact them. However, only those who are scary enough in Seeming or costume are allowed in. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Sites of Note</b></div> <br /> <b>Guillotine Plaza</b> - Also known as the Town Square of Halloween Town, this place is where the local hobgoblins and changelings gather to converse and conduct &quot;political&quot; business. It's centered by the massive guillotine that it takes its name after, which is used ceremoniously at the beginning of every Halloween night by chopping off the head of a citizen decided by lottery. But rather than killing the chosen victim outright, it merely decapitates them, using the power of the Wyrd to keep them alive as they experience lightheaded fun and play around with their disembodied head, which can be reattached at anytime--though only to the body it was cut from. Traditionally, users of this token are meant to ride a nightmare horse about the town, with head in hand, to scare away hostile creatures from the Hedge. This reenactment of the Headless Horseman is considered a high honor, and generally grants status with the local hobs.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hangman's Tree</b> - Nearby to Guillotine Plaza, this seemingly dead tree has an assortment of dead bodies ever hung by the neck to its branches. However, when a changeling gets close enough to see the faces of the dead, they realize that they are friends, family and even enemies they know to be dead. If a changeling feeds the tree glamour (1 per corpse) the body animates and can answer a question. If anyone tries to remove one of the cadavers, the tree itself animates to reveal a monstrous face on its trunk and warns against the action, and will attack if ignored. However, should a corpse be removed from the tree, it turns out to be merely a mannequin--but a rather realistic one that acts as a special kind of token.<br /> <br /> <b>Finkelstein's Lab</b> - Home to a reclusive hob, this tower overlooking Halloween Town is a place of &quot;Wyrd Science,&quot; where Finkelstein attempts to tap into the raw power of the Hedge via a mixture of alchemy, occult mysticism, and more. The tower is also prone to lightning strikes, much to the hob's delight.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hinterlands</b> - Just like the rest of the hedge settlement, the Hinterlands reflect the elements of fear in the form of a dead forest that has merged with the thorns and bramble of the hedge. Although empty by day, the forest is haunted by various creatures at night, and in a realm where time is fickle it can become dangerous to simply walk into. Despite the danger, rumors abound that there exists trees with doors built into them, each leading to a place similar to Halloween Town in that they celebrate a holiday everyday. But still, they're just rumors, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Moonlight Hill</b> - Perhaps one of the most hauntingly beautiful places in Halloween Town, this hill is made from the curl of both grave soil merged with thornless bramble. Surrounding it is a cemetery and pumpkin patch--these pumpkins being goblin fruit that the town harvests for the numerous feasts they have. But it is during the late of night, when the hill is bathed in moonlight, that its true beauty is seen, and is generally the place people go to when they need time away from the festivities. <div align=\"center\"><b>Denizens</b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack Skellington, the Pumpkin King</b><br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>&quot;My dearest friend, if you don't mind... I'd like to join you by your side.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Background:</b><br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 5, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Holidays) 4, Crafts 2, Investigation 3, Occult 4, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Stealth 4,<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken (Canines) 2, Expression (Oratory) 4, Intimidation (Shock) 5, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Giant \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Hedge Gate Sense \u2022, Enchanting Performance \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Fighting Style: Hedge Duelist \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Charity<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> 5<br /> <b>Contracts:</b> Fleeting Autumn \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Spell-Bound Autumn \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Darkness \u2022\u2022, Separation \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Smoke \u2022<br /> <b>Glamour/per Turn</b> 14/5<br /> <b>Armor:</b> None<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks:</b><br /> <br /> Pending...<br /> <br /> <b>Oogie-Boogie, the Boogieman</b><br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>&quot;When Mr. Oogie Boogie says there's trouble close at hand, you'd better pay attention now 'cause I'm the Boogie Man!&quot;</i><br /> <b>Background:</b> Halloween Town is not immune to the horrors of the True Fae. Despite it's entertaining atmosphere, there's always one thing that threatens the stability of the hedge town: the boogieman himself. A trickster and a cheater, Oogie-Boogie visits Halloween Town on the night of the new moon, his business never truly known. In the hedge, he appears as an obese humanoid figure made from a sack that has something crawling beneath its surface, but even if one looks into the eye and mouth holes of his head, all they will see is mirthful darkness. In the mortal realm, Oogie appears as a large man with glowing white teeth that make a rather unnerving grin. He enjoys playing in casinos, nightclubs and playgrounds, where he can best scope out potential victims.<br /> Regarding his changelings, he usually has his three loyalists, Shock, Lock, and Barrel, to kidnap potential servants, the Gentry only bothering to go when he needs to replace a would-be changeling with a fetch. One thing all citizens of Halloween Town warn newcomers of is that they should never play a game with Oogie, as if you lose, he'll through you into his mouth and walk back to Arcadia with you, the sensation of squirming insects all you'll ever remember after being inside.<br /> Of these changelings, Oogie generally creates Darklings, but Wizened Gamers are also common, as he loves to play rigged games of chance, and also Fairest Dancers, since he generally dances with them to his own singing.<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Hope<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust<br /> <b>Health/Willpower/Wyrd:</b> 7/3/6<br /> <b>Mein Blessings:</b> Immortal Flesh, Ruled by Passion, Slither and Squirm (Tunnel Grub), Fae Grace (Dancer), Smell the Blood (Cyclopean)<br /> <b>Frailties:</b> Hearing the sound of silver bells (minor taboo), being seen in broad daylight (major taboo)<br /> Intelligence/Wits/Resolve: 2/2/1<br /> Strength/Dexterity/Stamina: 2/3/2<br /> Presence/Manipulation/Composure: 5/2/2<br /> <b>Contracts:</b><br /> Fleeting Autumn \u2013 5<br /> Darkness \u2013 5<br /> Smoke \u2013 3<br /> Hearth \u2013 5<br /> Dreams \u2013 3<br /> Moon - 2<br /> Fang &amp; Talon - (Insects) 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Giant \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Barfly \u2022, Danger Sense \u2022\u2022, Token (Bone Dice) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Skills:</b><br /> Mental: Crafts 3, Occult 3,<br /> Physical: Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Stealth 5, Survival 2<br /> Social: Expression (Singing) 3, Intimidation 5, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge (Cheating) 4<br /> </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_postfooter text_table_content_tr text_table_postContainer_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_small text_table_postTop text_table_content_td text_table_postContainer_td text_table_postfooter_td\" colspan=\"3\"></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 10-18-2014, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T11:02:58-07:00","id":286036,"title":"","content":"<br /> Oogie\u00b4s Wyrd rating (his Actor\u00b4s)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T11:20:49-07:00","id":286042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/285890-goblin-hedge-settlement-halloween-town?p=286036#post286036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oogie\u00b4s Wyrd rating (his Actor\u00b4s)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote it as 6. Right next to Health and Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<b